{
  // Die-only import: the STEP file holds just the two gear-blank dies. The workpiece is defined in the app.
  // Workpiece sizes and the sweep values below are in mm (the app converts them to the selected units).
  "title": "7 · Die-only import: size, orient and place your own workpiece",
  "level": "Intermediate · 3D · STEP import (dies only) · a few minutes per run",
  "summary": "Import only the gear-blank dies, then design the workpiece yourself: round bar or block, on end or lying flat, centred or off-centre.",
  "instructions": [
    "1. The STEP file contains two bodies, the gear-blank dies, so the app asks for the moving die and then lets you define the workpiece. It is pre-set to a Ø56 × 81 mm bar standing on end (about 80 % of the cavity volume). Runs take a few minutes: off-centre and flat workpieces trigger extra local refinement.",
    "2. Basic tab → Workpiece: press 'Size to cavity +10 %' to give the bar the usual flash allowance. The preview updates as you type; the bar is always dropped onto the bottom die.",
    "3. Press Solve and note peak load and fill. Then try a HorizontalBar (rotate it with 'Rotation about press axis') and a Block, and compare the runs in RUNS: the same volume, but very different flow and flash.",
    "4. Placement matters: set Position X to 5 or 10 mm and solve again. Turn on View ▾ → Flow arrows and Die contact to watch the hub fill late on one side and the flash run unevenly.",
    "5. Run its multi-run: it sweeps the workpiece position X (0, 4, 8, 12 mm) so you can chart how sensitive fill and load are to an off-centre billet.",
    "6. Save setup… stores the workpiece with the job, so the same billet comes back when you reopen or re-import the dies."
  ],
  "setup": {
    "analysis": "3D",
    "stepFile": "../sample_gear_dies_only.step",
    "topDieBody": 2,
    "workpiece": { "shape": "VerticalBar", "diameter": 56, "length": 81, "angleDeg": 0, "offsetX": 0, "offsetY": 0 },
    "material": "AISI 4140",
    "temperature": 1150,
    "friction": 0.3,
    "elementSize": 4,
    "strokeIncrement": 0.8,
    "ramSpeed": 50,
    "pressCapacity": 2000
  },
  "sweep": { "parameter": "WorkpieceOffsetX", "values": [ "0", "4", "8", "12" ] }
}
